Problem 1 — Finding Updated Records

Platform: StrataScratch
Concept: Subquery in FROM using ROW_NUMBER window function
Task: From an employee salary table that may contain duplicate records, return only the most recent (highest salary) record per employee ID.
Logic: The inner query ranks each employee's records by salary (descending). The outer query filters to only the top-ranked row per employee.


SELECT id, first_name, last_name, department_id, salary
FROM (
SELECT *,
ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY id ORDER BY salary DESC, department_id DESC) AS rn
FROM ms_employee_salary
) s
WHERE rn = 1
ORDER BY id ASC;
